.\" The manual page for soliterm. See how it reads with: man -l man/soliterm.6
.\" The GAMES section lists every game, so a new game needs a line here too.
.TH SOLITERM 6 2026-09-29 "Soliterm 1.1.0" "Games Manual"
.\" never break these names across lines
.hw soliterm AisleRiot
.SH NAME
soliterm \- solitaire in the terminal, played by AisleRiot's rules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.ad l
.B soliterm
.RB [ \-\-game
.IR game ]
.RB [ \-\-deal
.IR number | code
.RB "| " \-\-daily ]
.RB [ \-\-draw
.BR 1 | 3 ]
.RB [ \-\-suits
.BR 1 | 2 | 4 ]
.RB [ \-\-text ]
.RB [ \-\-ascii ]
.RB [ \-\-color " | " \-\-no\-color ]
.RB [ \-\-theme
.IR theme ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-animation ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-sync ]
.PP
.B soliterm
.BR \-\-list " | " \-\-stats " | " \-\-debug\-info
.PP
.B soliterm \-\-reset\-stats
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.PP
.B soliterm
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.ad
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soliterm
plays thirteen solitaire card games in a terminal, with the keyboard or the
mouse.
It plays each one the way GNOME AisleRiot does, scoring and all, and when
AisleRiot is installed the two keep one record between them of the games
won and played and the best and worst times, so a game won in either
shows up in both.
.PP
With no options it opens a menu of the games.
Every deal has a number, shown on the board, and a share code such as
.B klondike:d3:48213
names a deal along with its options, so anyone can play the same cards.
The daily deal of each game is the same for everyone that day, with no
network involved.
A game you leave unfinished with
.BR q ,
.B m
or Ctrl-C, or by closing the terminal, is kept for next time, and picking
that game again carries on where you left off.
On Windows, a game left by closing the console window or with Ctrl-Break
is kept too.
If
.B soliterm
is ended some other way, as
.B taskkill /f
does, the game in play is neither kept nor counted, though if it was
picked up from a save, that save is offered again next time, as it was
when picked up.
.PP
Text mode plays the same games as plain lines of text.
It prints the board, reads one command a line from standard input, and
prints the board again, so it works in a pipe, in a script and on a
terminal curses can't drive.
.B soliterm
plays in text mode when
.B \-\-text
is given, when its input or output isn't a terminal, when curses can't be
loaded, or when
.B TERM
names no terminal it can draw on, and in the last two cases it says why
on standard error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short summary of the options and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-game " game"
Start
.I game
instead of the menu.
.I game
is one of the keys listed under
.B GAMES
and by
.BR \-\-list ,
such as
.BR klondike .
.TP
.BI \-\-deal " number\fR|\fPcode"
Play deal
.IR number ,
from 0 to 2147483647, or the deal a share code names.
A share code carries its game and options with it, as
.B klondike:d3:48213
is Klondike drawing three.
A number on its own plays that deal of the game given with
.BR \-\-game ,
or of the game last played, with your usual options for it.
FreeCell's numbers are the ones Microsoft FreeCell uses.
After a numbered deal,
.B n
deals the next number.
.TP
.B \-\-daily
Play today's daily deal of the game given with
.BR \-\-game ,
or of the game last played.
It always has the standard options.
.TP
.BR "\-\-draw 1" | 3
Klondike: draw one card at a time or three, for this run only.
Given without
.BR \-\-game ,
it plays Klondike.
.TP
.BR "\-\-suits 1" | 2 | 4
Spider: play with one, two or four suits, for this run only.
Given without
.BR \-\-game ,
it plays Spider.
.TP
.B \-\-text
Play in text mode even at a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Show the suits as the letters S, H, D and C instead of their symbols, and
draw the cards with plain ASCII.
.B soliterm
does this on its own when the terminal or the output can't show the
symbols.
.TP
.B \-\-color
Colour the cards in text mode even when the output isn't a terminal, and
turn colour on in the full-screen game whatever
.B NO_COLOR
or the saved setting says.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Leave out colour, in either mode, for this run.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " theme"
Draw the full-screen game in
.IR theme ,
one of
.BR classic ,
.BR dark ,
.B light
and
.BR contrast ,
for this run only.
The
.B t
key moves on to the next theme and keeps it.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-animation
Send the cards up at the finish, and leave them be after a win, without
animating them.
.B \(dqanimation\(dq: false
in
.I config.json
does the same for good.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List the games, with their keys, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Print the statistics of every game, with the win streaks and the last ten
games played, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-reset\-stats
Erase the statistics of every game and the history of games played, and
exit.
When statistics are shared, AisleRiot's own record of these games is
erased too.
It asks first, and keeps a backup of each file it clears.
Saved games stay where they are.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
With
.BR \-\-reset\-stats ,
clear the statistics without asking.
Without a terminal to ask at,
.B \-\-reset\-stats
needs it.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-info
Print what a bug report needs: the versions of
.B soliterm
and Python, the terminal, curses and where the files are.
It only reads, and changes nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sync
Leave AisleRiot's statistics alone this time.
The games played are kept in
.BR soliterm 's
own record, and go into AisleRiot's with the next game that's shared.
.SH GAMES
.TP
.B klondike
Klondike: the classic one-deck game, with seven columns and a stock,
drawing one card or three.
.TP
.B spider
Spider: two decks and ten columns, where full King to Ace runs clear
away, in one, two or four suits.
.TP
.B spiderette
Spiderette: Spider on one deck and seven columns, dealt like Klondike.
.TP
.B freecell
FreeCell: every card face up, four free cells, and nearly every deal can
be won.
.TP
.B eightoff
Eight Off: FreeCell with eight cells and columns built down in suit.
.TP
.B golf
Golf: clear seven columns onto the waste, one rank up or down.
.TP
.B triplepeaks
Triple Peaks: clear three overlapping peaks onto the waste, one rank up
or down, King and Ace next to each other.
.TP
.B yukon
Yukon: Klondike with no stock, where any face-up group of cards can move.
.TP
.B scorpion
Scorpion: seven columns built down in suit, any face-up group moves, and
the runs clear away.
.TP
.B bakersdozen
Bakers Dozen: thirteen open columns and no stock, built down by rank.
.TP
.B fortythieves
Forty Thieves: two decks, ten columns built down in suit, and one pass
through the stock.
.TP
.B canfield
Canfield: a reserve of thirteen, three cards dealt at a time, and
foundations that start from a rank the deal picks.
.TP
.B pyramid
Pyramid, AisleRiot's Thirteen: take a pyramid apart in pairs that make
13, a King on its own, with one pass through the stock.
.SH KEYS
These are the keys on the board of the full-screen game.
.B ?
shows them there, and
.I docs/keybindings.md
has the keys of every screen.
.TP
.BR Arrows ", " k ", " j ", " l
Move the cursor between the piles.
.TP
.BR Enter ", " Space
Pick up the cards at the cursor, and press again on another pile to put
them down.
In Golf and Triple Peaks, a card that goes on the waste is played there.
In Pyramid, put a card down on the one it makes 13 with to take both
off.
.TP
.BR + ", " \-
Lift one card more, or one fewer, while holding a run.
.TP
.B Esc
Put the cards back, or clear the hint.
.TP
.B d
Deal from the stock.
.TP
.B a
Send up every card that's safe to send up, or, once every card left can
go up, finish the game.
.TP
.B f
Send the card at the cursor to its foundation.
In Pyramid it takes off a King, or the top two cards of the waste when
they make 13.
.TP
.B h
Show a hint.
.TP
.BR u ", " r
Undo and redo a move.
.B U
and
.B R
undo or redo every move.
.TP
.BR n ", " N
Deal a new game, or start this one over.
.TP
.B g
Play a deal by its number or share code.
.TP
.BR o ", " s ", " ?
The options of this game, the statistics, and help.
.TP
.BR m ", " q
Back to the menu, or quit.
A game under way is kept for next time.
.TP
.BR b ", " F2
Boss mode: hide the game behind something that looks like work.
.TP
.BR c ", " x
The code skin, which plays the game inside a source file, and the compact
view.
.TP
.BR v ", " t ", " 4
Colour on or off, the next theme, and the four-colour deck.
.PP
With the mouse, click a card to pick it up along with the cards on it,
then click where it goes, or drag it there.
A double-click sends a card up to its foundation, or deals from the
stock.
In Golf and Triple Peaks, a click on a card that goes on the waste plays
it there.
In Pyramid, a double-click takes off a King.
.PP
In text mode, a slot is named by the number in its tag on the board, and
.B 12 2
moves cards from slot 12 to slot 2.
.B h
lists the other commands, and
.I docs/text-mode.md
explains them.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/soliterm/config.json
The settings: each game's options, the colours and theme, the game last
played, and
.BR sync_aisleriot ,
which turns sharing with AisleRiot off for good when set to
.BR false .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/soliterm/stats.json
The statistics of every game.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/soliterm/history.jsonl
A line for every game played, which the streaks and
.B \-\-stats
come from.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/soliterm/saves/
The games kept for next time, one file for each game.
A game picked up from one stays there, under another name, while it's
played, so one lost to a crash is offered again next time, as it was
when picked up.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gnome\-games/aisleriot
AisleRiot's own statistics, which
.B soliterm
shares when AisleRiot is installed.
It only ever changes the statistics of the games it has, and leaves the
rest of the file as it was.
AisleRiot reads the file once, when it starts, and can write its own copy
back over it when it quits.
A game finished in
.B soliterm
while AisleRiot is open is then lost from AisleRiot's statistics, and
from the same numbers in
.BR soliterm ,
so keep AisleRiot closed while playing
.BR soliterm .
On Linux,
.B soliterm
warns as the first game starts if AisleRiot is open, on the bottom line
or, in text mode, on standard error.
.PP
With
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
unset, the settings go in
.IR ~/.config ,
and with
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
unset, the rest goes in
.IR ~/.local/share .
On Windows,
.I ~
is the user's profile folder.
.PP
.B soliterm
used to be called aisle-cli.
The first time it runs, before it has folders of its own, it copies
.I config.json
and
.I stats.json
across from the
.I aisle\-cli
folders beside where its own go, and says so on standard error.
It copies them and never moves them, so the old files stay where they
were.
If aisle-cli was sharing its statistics with AisleRiot, its games aren't
added to AisleRiot's record a second time.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SOLITERM_NO_AISLERIOT
When set to anything but the empty string or
.BR 0 ,
leaves AisleRiot's statistics alone, as
.B \-\-no\-sync
does.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to anything but the empty string, turns colour off, as
.B \-\-no\-color
does.
.B \-\-color
still turns it on.
.TP
.B COLORFGBG
Some terminals, such as rxvt and Konsole, put their colours here.
When it ends in 7 or 15, a white background, the
.B classic
theme swaps the cyan and yellow of its titles, labels, messages and code
skin for darker colours, and
.B contrast
darkens its code skin.
.B dark
and
.B light
look the same whatever it says.
.TP
.B TERM
The terminal's type.
When it names a type with no terminfo entry,
.B soliterm
plays as
.BR xterm-256color ,
or
.B xterm
if that's the one there, and says so as the first game starts and on
stderr at the end.
Inside tmux or screen it plays as
.B screen-256color
or
.B screen
instead.
When it's unset, is
.BR dumb ,
names a type that can't move the cursor, or none of those is known
either,
.B soliterm
plays in text mode.
Windows doesn't use it.
.TP
.B ESCDELAY
How many milliseconds curses waits after Esc for the rest of a key.
.B soliterm
makes it 25 unless it's set.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME
Where the files go, as under
.BR FILES .
Pointing them at an empty directory gives a fresh start that leaves your
own files alone.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The game was won, or you left it, or the input ran out, or one of the
options that print something and exit did so.
.TP
.B 1
.B \-\-reset\-stats
cleared nothing, because the answer wasn't yes, a backup couldn't be made
or
.I stats.json
couldn't be written, or curses failed while the full-screen game was
running.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was wrong, or
.B \-\-reset\-stats
had no terminal to ask at and no
.BR \-\-yes .
.TP
.B 130
Ctrl-C, SIGHUP, SIGTERM or, on Windows, Ctrl-Break.
The game is kept or counted first, as it is for
.BR q ,
and at the
.B \-\-reset\-stats
prompt nothing is cleared.
.TP
.B 141
Whatever was reading the output stopped, as
.BR head (1)
does.
.PP
On Windows, closing the console window still ends
.B soliterm
with status 0xC000013A, but only once the game has been kept or counted.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open the menu:
.PP
.RS
.EX
soliterm
.EE
.RE
.PP
Play FreeCell deal 617, or a share code someone sent you:
.PP
.RS
.EX
soliterm \-\-game freecell \-\-deal 617
soliterm \-\-deal klondike:d3:48213
.EE
.RE
.PP
Play today's Spider daily deal:
.PP
.RS
.EX
soliterm \-\-daily \-\-game spider
.EE
.RE
.PP
Play Golf deal 216 in text mode, with letters for the suits:
.PP
.RS
.EX
soliterm \-\-text \-\-deal golf:216 \-\-ascii
.EE
.RE
.PP
Try something out without touching your statistics or AisleRiot's:
.PP
.RS
.EX
tmp=$(mktemp \-d)
XDG_CONFIG_HOME=$tmp XDG_DATA_HOME=$tmp soliterm \-\-no\-sync
.EE
.RE
.SH BUGS
Report them at https://github.com/bwenstar/soliterm/issues, with what
.B soliterm \-\-debug\-info
prints.
.PP
On Windows,
.B soliterm
has been tried in the classic console, conhost, on Windows Server 2025,
with Python 3.9 and 3.14 and windows-curses 2.4.2, but not yet in Windows
Terminal or on desktop Windows 10 or 11.
